cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this app, please cite the work it implements (preferred-citation), this release, and Pennsieve (RRID:SCR_021677); the other works it builds on are listed under references.
type: software
title: st-celltype
abstract: >-
  A Pennsieve processor for single-cell spatial transcriptomics (Xenium, MERSCOPE, CosMx, Visium HD
  bins): joint PCA, optional Harmony integration by sample, Leiden clustering, and marker-set
  scoring (scanpy score_genes) against a user marker table or a built-in canonical table drawn
  from PanglaoDB, calling a cell type per cluster or per cell; writes labels, cluster markers,
  scores, summaries and figures.
authors:
  - name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
repository-code: "https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/st-celltype"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - single-cell
  - cell typing
  - clustering
  - Xenium
  - MERSCOPE
  - CosMx
  - Leiden
  - Harmony
  - marker genes
# The work this app implements; the release report's "How to cite" puts it first.
